title: Who Controls the Treasury?
subtitle: Finance is a ministry, a veto point and KO's preferred border checkpoint.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and finance_minister_party = "Lewica" and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_fiscal_policy_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_fiscal_policy_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/events/finance-ministry.webp

= Who Controls the Treasury?

KO accepted a Left finance minister after harsh negotiations and now treats
every distributive decision as a test of whether that concession was a
mistake. The ministry's first real tax line will decide whether the office has
authority or merely a nameplate.

[? if left_is_junior_partner = 1: **[+ coalition_senior_partner +] holds the
premiership** and regards the Finance Ministry as a concession it can revisit.
Objection risk on a contested measure: **[+ coalition_objection_risk +]%**.?]

- @progressive_revenue
- @coalition_rule
- @publish_constraints

@progressive_revenue
title: Enforce a progressive revenue package
subtitle: Raise durable capacity and accept a hard liberal backlash — if the package survives the coalition at all.
on-arrival: {!
const objectionRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const objected =
    Q.left_is_junior_partner &&
    objectionRoll * 100 < Number(Q.coalition_objection_risk) * 1.15;
Q.last_card_objection = objected ? 1 : 0;
Q.last_card_objector = Q.coalition_senior_partner;
if (objected) {
    // What survives is enforcement against small payers, which raises less
    // and costs more politically than the package it replaced.
    Q.budget += 1;
    Q.fiscal_stress -= 1;
    Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
    Q.workers_support -= 1;
    Q.left_coalition_dissent += 6;
    Q.coalition_blur += 3;
    Q.ministry_overruled_count += 1;
    Q.ministry_overruled_last = "Progressive revenue package";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.coalition_senior_partner +
        " reduces the revenue package to an enforcement drive";
} else {
    Q.budget += 2;
    Q.fiscal_stress -= 3;
    Q.workers_support += 4;
    Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
    Q.public_service_families_left_affinity += 2;
    Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity -= 2;
    Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 6;
    Q.ko_relation -= 4;
    Q.ko_poll_momentum -= 0.15;
    Q.economic_growth -= 0.2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The Treasury shifts enforcement and relief toward a progressive tax settlement";
}
!}

Capital income, top earners and aggressive avoidance move to the front of the
programme. The numbers work. KO's ministers respond by making clear that
arithmetical coherence is not the same thing as coalition consent.

[? if last_card_objection = 1: What reaches the Sejm is the enforcement half:
more audits, more compliance staff, no new rate on capital income. The revenue
is smaller, the resentment is concentrated among people with one shop rather
than one portfolio, and the announcement still had our minister's name on
it.?]

- #poland_card_finish


@coalition_rule
title: Trade the package for a joint investment rule
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. A narrower settlement protects room for public investment.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Negotiating and defending a new fiscal rule requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; fiscal_stress -= 2; government_delivery += 3; ko_relation += 3; ko_coalition_dissent -= 2; budget_promises += 1; progressive_credibility -= 1; news_headline = "The coalition agrees a fiscal rule with protected investment space"

The Treasury gives up the headline confrontation in exchange for rules that
do not classify every hospital, railway and housing programme as identical
current spending. It is compromise with a ledger attached.

- #poland_card_finish


@publish_constraints
title: Publish the coalition's fiscal constraints
subtitle: Free fallback. Honest, and an admission that the ministry is a nameplate this quarter.
on-arrival: public_trust += 2; constitutional_restraint += 1; ko_relation += 1; government_delivery -= 1; progressives_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 2; household_policy_pressure += 3; coalition_blur += 2; last_card_objection = 0; news_headline = "The Treasury publishes what the coalition will and will not finance"

No tax line changes today. Instead, the ministry releases the assumptions,
vetoes and trade-offs behind the budget. KO avoids a defeat; the Left avoids
pretending that a liberal ceiling is a law of nature.

The document is also a public statement that our finance minister cannot
finance the programme we were elected on. Everyone who wanted that programme
reads it that way, because that is what it says.

- #poland_card_finish
